      "writtenOn": "2012-03-06T15:06:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way you have written this class, it does not actually seem necessary.  What is the behavior you are looking to swap  by changing the implementation?  Brain is,  of course, a horrible class name:  too cutesy,  and not really descriptive,  but I understand if you have trouble coming up with a better one,  I\u0027m guessing because this is not really a class but instead a function.\n\nIf I understand correctly,  this is supposed to be  an implementation of the Strategy pattern,  so you can choose different ways to enforce the rules.  However,  this is really a rules engine,  and just tells some other class  whether a given action is valid or not.  Gatekeeper, Guard,  or Monitor are all more descriptive names for this class.",
      "revId": "a564c6e141e2902c1159e0ae2f9646bb1d985a43",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
